<!--
    Legacy palette - the application's CURRENT colours, lifted verbatim.

    TRANSITIONAL, WITH A WRITTEN EXPIRY AND A NAMED OWNER FOR IT.
    Keys are named for the role each colour OBSERVABLY plays today - read off the
    attribute it appears in and the surfaces it is drawn on - never for the role it will
    play in 3a. Naming these for their final 3a role and flipping only the values later
    was considered and rejected: seven of these colours (the greens, the violet, the warm
    orange, the History-tab gold trio) have NO Broadsheet counterpart, and collapsing them
    now would change pixels. T-001's acceptance bar is pixel-equivalence.

    The `broadsheet:` note on each entry is the map forward. T-003 through T-009 rebind
    their surfaces to the Broadsheet key as they rebuild them; T-009 - the last task in
    the epic to touch a rendered surface - DELETES this file and Legacy.Metrics.xaml.
    (T-001's spec body says T-011; the coherence pass reassigned it to T-009 and that
    amendment governs. See docs/todo/T-001.md "Coherence amendments".)

    Every value here is the value that shipped. If one differs from git HEAD before
    T-001, this file is wrong.
-->
